  "label": "Single Cell Spatial Tumor Heterogeneity",
  "related": [
    "mouse-glial-9399",
    "epidemiological-compartmental-3094",
    "plant-notoginseng-7d04"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "systems"
  ],
  "slug": "cancer-associated-9fd1",
  "summary": "Single-cell and spatial multi-omics in these studies map intratumoral heterogeneity, epithelial remodelling, and immunosuppressive niches across cancer types.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of single-cell and spatial methods to resolve tumour heterogeneity and link it to molecular states, microenvironmental composition, and metabolic programmes. Single-nucleus ATAC-seq in colorectal cancer distinguishes iCMS2 and iCMS3 as epigenomic states driven by divergent cis-regulatory activity, and ovarian high-grade serous carcinoma shows intra- and intertumor heterogeneity by scRNA-seq and spatial transcriptomics. In pancreatic cancer, OTUD7B drives epithelial remodelling and an immunosuppressive microenvironment, and transcription factor-defined glycolytic and lipogenic subtypes carry distinct prognostic features. Spatial proteomics quantifies single-cell intratumoral drug distribution and barriers, while melanoma studies span T-cell organisation in lymph node metastases and AI-guided histopathology. Not all items share this thread; the metabolic, mutational-burden, and epigenetic reviews are adjacent. What is new is single-cell and spatial resolution coupled to mechanistic and prognostic readouts.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-02"
}
